(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-checker/src/check.asl#Deferred.args" :text "Argument types")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-checker/src/check.asl#Deferred.result" :text "Result type")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-checker/src/check.asl#genericSig" :text "D159: a multi-type generic name takes a fresh variable until its receiver is known; a one-type name has its concrete builtin's signature.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-checker/src/check.asl#mantissaOk?" :text "digits, or digits.digits (ASL1-floatExponentLiteral: shared by the mantissa of a plain or exponent float).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-checker/src/check.asl#expOk?" :text "an exponent's own optional sign and digits, e.g. the +5 of 1e+5 (ASL1-floatExponentLiteral).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-checker/src/check.asl#splitExp" :text "mantissa and exponent digits split at the first e or E, same host grammar as reader.c's classifyNumber (ASL1-floatExponentLiteral); no e or E, or more than one, leaves the exponent none so the caller's own digit check rejects the whole token.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-checker/src/check.asl#isFloatLit?" :text "digits.digits, digits[eE][+-]digits or digits.digits[eE][+-]digits (ASL1-floatExponentLiteral: asl1 now lexes the same exponent grammar read.c's classifyNumber accepts, e.g. 1e22, 1.5e-3, -2E+5).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-checker/src/check.asl#paramAnnText" :text "The raw type annotation text of a lambda parameter, empty when unannotated; feeds the implicit single-letter typevar scan that lambdaTypeBound does.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-checker/src/check.asl#lambdaTypeBound" :text "Single-uppercase-letter names in a lambda's own annotation text are implicit type params (CHECKERTYPENAME), same convention collectSummary uses for defun signatures.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-checker/src/check.asl#addTypeTreeDiags" :text "Runs the module-level unknown-type check (resolve/checkTypeTree, rule-10) against a lambda's own annotation, which collectSummary never sees.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-checker/src/check.asl#checkLambdaAnnText" :text "Validates a lambda's own raw, unqualified annotation text (CHECKERTYPENAME); checkTypeTree does its own alias lookup, so this must run on the type parsed straight from source, never on a qualifyTypeWithMod result (that rewrites the alias to the target module's name and makes checkTypeTree's own alias lookup fail). A blank text means no annotation was given, so there is nothing to check.")
